0042:     """
0043:     Rotate each blue-started chain of bottom-aligned vertical bars into horizontal bars resting on the same baseline.
0044:     Input structure
0045:     - The grid has a background and bottom-aligned, one-cell-wide vertical bars.
0046:     - Blue bars are markers; red bars are body bars that may be chained after a marker.
0047:     Rule
0048:     - Starting at each blue bar, repeatedly include the next red bar whose column is exactly the current bar's column plus the current bar's height.
0049:     - Clear every included vertical bar, then redraw each included bar horizontally to the right from its original bottom cell, with length equal to its vertical height.
0050:     - Red bars that are not reached from a blue marker remain unchanged.
0051:     Key insight
0052:     - A vertical bar's height is also the width it occupies after rotation, so the chain follows immediate horizontal contact after each rotated bar.
0053:     """
